      </ul>

      <h2>5. Retirement Parity: Pensions, Gratuity, and Commutation Standards</h2>
      <p>
        Pay Commission enhancements extend directly to retired veterans and surviving family dependents:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pension Parity:</strong> In accordance with statutory provisions, full basic pension entitlement is pegged at 50% of the last drawn basic pay. Past retirees receive pension revisions via the direct fitment multiplier, maintaining complete parity with active employees.</li>
        <li><strong>Gratuity Ceiling Expansion:</strong> While the death-cum-retirement gratuity ceiling was raised to ₹25 Lakhs under the 7th CPC after DA crossed 50%, recommendations for the 8th Pay Commission are expected to propose raising the maximum gratuity ceiling to between <strong>₹30 Lakhs and ₹40 Lakhs</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Commutation Period Restoration Demands:</strong> A primary demand submitted by pensioner associations to the Ministry of Finance is reducing the commuted pension recovery period from 15 years down to 12 years, citing current mortality indices and lower prevailing interest rates.</li>
      </ul>

